*~
*.pyc
*.pyo
.venv/
.coverage
mozdata.ini
# bugzilla.allizom.org API key, used to test the bug-filing writes against staging.
# A real credential sitting in the repo root: keep it one `git add -A` away from NOTHING.
.allizom
test.py
server.crt
server.csr
server.key
local.json

# Fetched at build time by bin/post_compile (Heroku); never commit these.
bin/searchfox-cli
.profile.d/searchfox-cli.sh

# spike/ is the scratch yard: throwaway probes, corpus dumps and one-off measurement
# scripts. A single session can leave 150+ files there, and spike/_dossier_dump.jsonl alone
# is 42 MB of prod agent output. Ignoring the directory wholesale keeps `git status`
# readable; it does NOT untrack anything already committed there, so the reports and tools
# worth keeping stay under version control as they are.
#
# To keep a NEW spike artifact — a report a handoff points at, a reusable tool — add it
# explicitly with `git add -f spike/<file>`.
spike/

# Phase-2 calibration eval artifacts (regenerable via eval.study_corpus / eval.calibrate).
corpus_*/
metrics_*.json

# Session working notes and handoffs. Deliberately untracked: they are scratch prose, not
# project docs, and a blanket `git add -A` swept them in twice (6292eea, b116551).
# This lived in .git/info/exclude, which is LOCAL-ONLY — a fresh clone lost the rule and the
# next blanket add would sweep them again. Listed here so the rule travels with the repo.
# Note this ignores them, it does not back them up: a handoff worth keeping must be
# committed explicitly with `git add -f`.
/clouseau_fenix.md
/find_authors.md
/jens_feedback_bug2065373.md
/next_session.md
/mccr8_reply_draft.md
/plans/16-fenix-nightly-support.md
/plans/17-dedup-beyond-the-signature.md
